THE FIX — VERIFIED SOUND. The reasoning about behaviours 5/6 is correct.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The stated invariant is the right one: on the `--ref` path the exclusion
must be what the DIRECT path would have computed with repo = the checkout
`--studio` really is nested under. `ci` computes exactly that
(toPosixRelative(root, resolve(studioArg ?? "."))), and `resolve(studioArg
?? ".")` matches `verify`'s own default (`let studio = "."`), so the two
paths cannot diverge on a missing --studio either.

Verified in three configurations, not one:

  (i)  studio nested in the repo (the real layout, and behaviour 8's):
       ref and direct front matters byte-identical. This is the case the
       bug lived in.
  (ii) studio outside the repo (behaviours 5/6's layout): both paths
       compute the SAME non-matching "../…" entry, so both exclude
       nothing and both agree. No new divergence is introduced — which is
       why 5 and 6 could never have caught the bug, exactly as claimed.
  (iii) studio nested but NOT named "studio" (I ran the fixture with the
       officina at <repo>/officina):
         ref    tree:49f5910c…   direct tree:49f5910c…   MATCH
       The fix generalises; it is not tuned to the name.

Mutation, on the mechanism the certificate now rests on — BOTH SIDES BITE.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Each applied alone to the clean worktree, full ci.test.ts run:

  M1  verify.ts: `opts.studioRepoRelative ?? toPosixRelative(repo, studioDir)`
      -> `toPosixRelative(repo, studioDir)`   (override ignored — pre-fix verify)
        behaviour 8 FAIL; 1-6 all PASS.
  M2  ci.ts: `toPosixRelative(root!, studioDirActual)`
      -> `toPosixRelative(execRepo, studioDirActual)`   (pre-fix ci)
        behaviour 8 FAIL; 1-6 all PASS.
  M3  ci.ts: the whole expression -> the literal `"studio"`
        behaviour 8 PASS — SURVIVES. See advisory A1.

M1 and M2 are the two independent ways the fix can be undone, and
behaviour 8 is the only thing in the suite that catches either. The
mechanism is covered from both ends.

